# =============================================================================
# RunPod pod template — Zion's Light AI
# =============================================================================
# Paste the KEY=VALUE lines below into the RunPod template's Environment
# Variables box. Kept in the repo so a terminated pod never costs you the
# config again (it has, twice).
#
# POD SETTINGS (not env vars — set these in the template UI):
#   Container Image ....... angreg/zions-light-ai:v3.1.6-cu12
#   Container Disk ........ 60 GB
#   Volume Mount Path ..... /data          <- attach the zions-data Network Volume
#   Expose HTTP Ports ..... 3000, 8080
#   Docker Command ........ (leave empty)
#
# Ports 8000 (vLLM), 9000 (STT), 9001 (TTS) stay internal — OpenWebUI reaches
# them over localhost. Do not expose them.
#
# IMAGE VARIANTS:
#   :v3.0-cu12   CUDA-12 / vLLM 0.19.0 — runs on ANY A40 host (driver >=525)
#   :v3.0-cu13   CUDA-13 / vLLM 0.24.0 — needs a driver >=580 host, zero CVEs (archived, not yet pod-validated)
# =============================================================================

# --- THE ONES THAT MATTER MOST ------------------------------------------------
# WEBUI_SECRET_KEY is the only var that strictly MUST be set. The model pair
# below matches the image's built-in default as of rc8 (before rc8 the default
# was a 22B that could not boot on an A40) — kept pinned EXPLICITLY so a future
# default change can never silently swap the production model under a deploy.

# Production-validated A40 config.
# 2026-08-24: corrected to the VISION variant. This file previously named the
# text-only repo, which would have silently disabled vision on a pod rebuild —
# backend_is_multimodal() (main.py:158) resolves False for it, images are
# replaced with a placeholder, and nothing errors. Confirm against the live pod
# with `echo $MODEL_REPO` before relying on this for a rebuild.
MODEL_REPO=coder3101/Cydonia-24B-v4.3-vision-heretic

# A 24B needs runtime fp8 (~43GB serving incl. KV) on a 48GB card; bf16 will
# not fit. Empty this if you switch to a 12B model or an 80GB card.
#
# --mm-processor-cache-type shm added 2026-09-01, and it is NOT optional
# while COMPACTOR_MAX_RETAINED_IMAGES > 0. vLLM's default multimodal cache
# is (its own docstring) a MIRRORED LRU: the API server keeps a copy of what
# it believes the engine core has cached and ships only the hash for those.
# When the engine restarts under a live API server the mirror goes stale, and
# the next request referencing that hash dies on
#     assert mm_item is not None  (vllm/multimodal/cache.py)
# mid-generation, as a 500. Observed 2026-09-01: the second image posted in a
# conversation failed every time, and OpenWebUI papered over the 500 with
# filler text, so it read as the model repeating itself.
#
# `shm` is a single shared-memory store instead of a sender/receiver pair, so
# there is no mirror to desynchronise. It also HALVES the memory: the default
# duplicates mm_processor_cache_gb (4) per API and engine process.
# Trade-off: shm is FIFO, not LRU. Dumber eviction, irrelevant at this scale.
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--quantization fp8 --mm-processor-cache-type shm

# MUST be a real value. Empty => regenerated every boot => everyone logged out.
# Generate one:  openssl rand -hex 32
WEBUI_SECRET_KEY=CHANGE_ME_openssl_rand_hex_32

# A HARD PRECONDITION of every v3.1.9 deploy (CHANGELOG.md [3.1.9]). Write it
# as exactly `false`. A MISSING OR EMPTY ROW STILL MEANS true — the database
# gets moved to local disk, which is the v3.1.9.1 feature, NOT supported on
# v3.1.9 (entrypoint.sh's own normalization: `1`/`yes`/`on`/`True` also mean
# true; `0`/`no`/`off` mean false; anything else refuses to boot with a
# `REFUSING TO START` banner rather than guess). After boot, the RunPod Logs
# tab must show `WEBUI_DB_LOCAL=false (explicitly set (false))` — see
# RUNPOD_DEPLOY.md "WEBUI_DB_LOCAL — a hard deploy precondition".
WEBUI_DB_LOCAL=false

# 6h instead of the 24h default — shrinks the data-loss window after the
# 2026-08-10 network-volume incident.
COMPACTOR_BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=6

# --- Model / inference -------------------------------------------------------
MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.90

# --- Context compactor -------------------------------------------------------
# COMPACTOR_TARGET_TOKENS empty => auto (75% of the HARD INPUT LIMIT, i.e.
# 75% of MAX_MODEL_LEN - COMPACTOR_GENERATION_RESERVE = 15576 at these values).
# Omitted here deliberately; RunPod handles empty values inconsistently.
# Do NOT set it above the hard input limit: compaction would never fire before
# the guard, and the guard can only DELETE turns where compaction would have
# summarized them. That is the 2026-08-28 failure.
COMPACTOR_KEEP_RECENT_TURNS=4
COMPACTOR_SUMMARY_MAX_TOKENS=1024
COMPACTOR_SUMMARY_INPUT_RESERVE=2048
# 2026-08-28: raised from 2048. Assistant replies here measure 7,513-11,347
# tokens; 2048 truncates them whenever a prompt reaches the ceiling.
#
# 16384 -> 12000 on 2026-09-01, to MATCH THE RUNNING POD. This file said
# 16384 while production ran 12000, so a rebuild from this template would
# have silently cut the input window from 20,768 to 16,384 - about two
# exchanges of her context, lost on deploy day with nothing to point at.
# Exactly the divergence that made MAX_RETAINED_IMAGES an incident: a value
# set live, never written down, reverted by the next build.
#
# 12000 is sized on measurement, not preference. Her replies (n=334,
# 2026-09-01 backup) run a median of 1,684 tokens, p90 4,436, max 12,822.
# Lowering this buys input context roughly 1 exchange per 2,000 tokens
# freed, at the cost of truncating her longest replies - one already hit
# finish_reason=length. Do not cut it without checking that p90 again.
COMPACTOR_GENERATION_RESERVE=12000

# --- Offline operation -------------------------------------------------------
# The pod must be able to BOOT and RUN with no internet. Everything it needs is
# already local: weights under HF_HOME on /data, the bge-small embedding model
# baked into the image at /opt/embeddings, and vLLM served over localhost.
#
# entrypoint.sh now treats an unreachable huggingface.co as a supported state
# whenever the cache is populated, and exports these itself. Setting them here
# as well pins the behaviour deliberately rather than leaving it to a probe:
# with them set, NOTHING on the request path can reach for the network.
#
# Why it matters beyond air-gapped deployment: transformers resolves MODEL_REPO
# against huggingface.co on the REQUEST path, and a soak run measured that
# blocking for 231 seconds on an HTTP 429. The weights were cached the whole
# time. (REMEDIATION F33 + F25.)
#
# Unset these only when deliberately changing models, and set them back after.


# --- Wall-clock time --------------------------------------------------------
# TZ sets the CONTAINER clock (what timestamps in the logs read as) ONLY.
# It is NOT read by the current-time-injection feature (v3.1.9) and never has
# been — main.py's _resolve_time_zone docstring says so explicitly ("TZ IS
# NOT READ"): the owner's precedence for what the MODEL is told is browser
# zone -> COMPACTOR_TIMEZONE (below) -> UTC, deliberately not TZ, because a
# second environment variable quietly feeding the clock is a source nobody
# would think to check when the time the model states is wrong. Leaving TZ
# set is harmless for what it actually does (log timestamps); do not expect
# it to affect what she is told the time is.
#
# tzdata IS in the image (/usr/share/zoneinfo), plus tzdata-legacy (v3.1.9,
# for old-style zone spellings like US/Arizona — see the Dockerfile comment).
TZ=America/Phoenix

# COMPACTOR_TIMEZONE — the model's clock while her chat is on `source=hash`
# (today's setup: no X-Conversation-Id header configured, see
# RUNBOOK_MEMORY_IDENTITY.md). With no identity header, the system prompt
# cannot safely carry `User timezone: {{CURRENT_TIMEZONE}}` (editing the
# system prompt on a hash-identity chat forks its memory — see
# RUNPOD_DEPLOY.md "The current date and time"), so the model is told this
# fixed zone instead of her browser's. It does NOT follow her if she
# travels; that needs header identity. Once her chat is on `source=header`
# and the system prompt carries the `User timezone:` line, this becomes a
# pure fallback (used only when the browser label is absent/invalid) and can
# stay set. Use the zone's CURRENT canonical name (America/Phoenix, not
# US/Arizona) unless you have confirmed tzdata-legacy resolves the old name
# on this image (hostile pass #5, reviewer A, F1). Empty/unset = UTC.
COMPACTOR_TIMEZONE=America/Phoenix

HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1
# Pins offline even when the network IS reachable. Belt and braces for a
# deployment that should never egress.
# COMPACTOR_FORCE_OFFLINE=true

# --- Memory: facts -----------------------------------------------------------
COMPACTOR_FACTS_EXTRACTION=true
COMPACTOR_FACTS_EXTRACTION_MAX_TOKENS=256

# TWO CAPS, TWO JOBS. They used to be one knob, and that was the bug.
#
# MAX_FACTS_TOKENS bounds the STORE: how much a conversation may remember
# on disk. Facts past it are evicted to a recoverable archive sidecar.
#
# v3.1.9: raised from the code default (1500) to 3500. The owner ran this
# live on the pod since v3.1.8 (a supervisord environment= edit, lost on
# every container restart) after measuring ~16 new facts/exchange with ~16
# evicted at 1500 (a churning store) and only 6-12 of ~160 stored facts
# actually reaching injection. v3.1.9 bakes it into the image/template so it
# survives a restart instead of needing to be reapplied by hand. See
# COMPACTOR_INJECTION_BUDGET_FRACTION below — it moved together with this
# and COMPACTOR_MAX_RETRIEVAL_TOKENS, not independently.
COMPACTOR_MAX_FACTS_TOKENS=3500
#
# INJECT_FACTS_TOKENS bounds what goes into THIS TURN'S PROMPT, ranked by
# relevance to what she just said. While these were the same number the
# entire active store was injected every turn, so every fact was touched
# every turn, so `last_used` carried no signal and eviction fell back to
# age - measured at 70% churn. It also fed the model ~164 fact bullets per
# request under a header asking it to stay consistent with them, which is
# a large part of why replies went formulaic (v3.1.6 F2; lexical variety
# fell 19% over the week it grew).
#
# THIS IS THE DIAL TO TURN IF SHE GOES TOO SPARSE after v3.1.6. Raising it
# gives her more of her own memory per turn at the cost of context for the
# conversation itself. Lowering it does the reverse. Code default 400;
# v3.1.9 raises it to 600 as part of the same pod-measured budget change
# as COMPACTOR_MAX_FACTS_TOKENS above.
COMPACTOR_INJECT_FACTS_TOKENS=600

# --- Memory: episodic / RAG --------------------------------------------------
COMPACTOR_RAG_ENABLED=true
COMPACTOR_RAG_TOP_K=5
# Token budget for the whole retrieved-exchange block. Retrieval was the one
# injected memory layer with NO cap — facts have MAX_FACTS_TOKENS, summaries
# have L1/L2/L3_MAX_TOKENS, retrieved exchanges were injected verbatim however
# long they were. Observed 2026-08-27: same conversation, 1retr and 0retr
# succeeded, 3retr produced a 33,127-token request against a 32,768 window on a
# payload compaction had already reduced to 9,915. Mirrors the facts budget on
# purpose — no memory layer should outweigh the conversation it supports.
#
# v3.1.9: raised from the code default (1500) to 3500, same pod-measured
# change as the facts rows above — with the owner's live traffic, retrieval
# kept only 1 of 5 candidate hits at 1500. See COMPACTOR_INJECTION_BUDGET_FRACTION
# below: this row's raise is the reason the fraction had to move too.
COMPACTOR_MAX_RETRIEVAL_TOKENS=3500
COMPACTOR_EMBEDDING_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5

# --- Memory: hierarchical summaries ------------------------------------------
COMPACTOR_HIERARCHICAL_SUMMARY=true
COMPACTOR_L1_CHUNK_SIZE=20
COMPACTOR_L2_CHUNK_SIZE=10
COMPACTOR_L3_CHUNK_SIZE=5
COMPACTOR_L1_MAX_TOKENS=500
COMPACTOR_L2_MAX_TOKENS=1200
COMPACTOR_L3_MAX_TOKENS=2000

# --- Memory: injection budget split ------------------------------------------
# inject_budget = effective_limit * COMPACTOR_INJECTION_BUDGET_FRACTION is
# shared by persona + summary + facts + retrieval (main.py). Code default
# 0.5 (~10,384 tokens on her 20,768-token window). v3.1.9 raises it to 0.6
# (~12,460 tokens) TOGETHER with the raised facts/retrieval caps above:
# retrieval is priority 3 and is dropped WHOLE when it does not fit
# (_bound_injected_blocks) — at 3500/3500 facts+retrieval caps but the OLD
# 0.5 fraction, retrieval would have been silently cut from every request.
# Do not raise COMPACTOR_MAX_FACTS_TOKENS / COMPACTOR_MAX_RETRIEVAL_TOKENS
# without raising this too, and vice versa.
COMPACTOR_INJECTION_BUDGET_FRACTION=0.6
# Summary block cap. Code default 12000 (summarizer.py) — v3.1.9 pins this
# LOWER, at 6230, which is what the summary block actually measured once it
# had room inside the 0.6 fraction above; it is not a further raise.
COMPACTOR_SUMMARY_BLOCK_MAX_TOKENS=6230

# --- Ops / durability --------------------------------------------------------
COMPACTOR_ADMIN_BIND=127.0.0.1
COMPACTOR_SELFTEST_ON_BOOT=true
COMPACTOR_BACKUP_ENABLED=true
COMPACTOR_BACKUP_DIR=/data/backups
# Interim raise from 7 (v3.1 §2.2). At INTERVAL_HOURS=6, RETAIN=7 was 42
# hours of total history: tightening the RPO after the 2026-08-10 incident
# without raising this shortened the recovery window from seven days to
# under two, and the 2026-08-24 incident took days to analyse. 28 restores
# roughly a week.
#
# SUPERSEDED by v3.1 F7: backup.py no longer treats this as a cap. Retention
# is by age (COMPACTOR_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAYS, default 14) plus a weekly GFS tier
# (COMPACTOR_BACKUP_GFS_WEEKS, default 8), and this value now acts only as an
# additional floor on the number kept. It can no longer cause a prune; raising
# it can only keep more.
COMPACTOR_BACKUP_RETAIN=28
# Retention tier defaults, shown for the runbook. Uncomment to override.
# COMPACTOR_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAYS=14
# COMPACTOR_BACKUP_GFS_WEEKS=8
# Hard floor on archives kept, whatever their age. backup.py floors this at 3
# in code — a typo here cannot empty /data/backups.
# COMPACTOR_BACKUP_MIN_KEEP=3
# Refuse to publish an archive whose payload is under this fraction of the
# previous one's (a half-empty store is an unmounted volume, not an edit).
# COMPACTOR_BACKUP_MIN_PAYLOAD_RATIO=0.5
COMPACTOR_BACKUP_MIN_FREE_MB=500
COMPACTOR_MIN_FREE_MB_WRITES=200
COMPACTOR_MAX_CONCURRENT_TAILS=4
COMPACTOR_MAX_OUTSTANDING_TAILS=64
COMPACTOR_LOG_FORMAT=text

# --- Voice (STT / TTS) -------------------------------------------------------
STT_ENABLED=true
WHISPER_MODEL=base
WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu
TTS_ENABLED=true
TTS_VOICE=en_US-lessac-medium

# --- OpenWebUI ---------------------------------------------------------------
WEBUI_AUTH=true

# SQLite hardening for the /data network volume (MooseFS). WAL needs an mmap'd
# -shm file that a distributed FS does not honor — leaving it on is what tore
# webui.db on 2026-08-10. Do NOT set WAL true unless /data is a real local disk.
DATABASE_ENABLE_SQLITE_WAL=false
DATABASE_SQLITE_PRAGMA_BUSY_TIMEOUT=10000
DATABASE_SQLITE_PRAGMA_MMAP_SIZE=0

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend modality: auto-detected from MODEL_REPO. Text-only models get
# uploaded images replaced with an honest placeholder (v3.0.1 fix).
# COMPACTOR_BACKEND_MULTIMODAL=auto
# Vision: cap retained images (v3.0.2) + per-image token estimate.
#   -1 = unlimited · 0 = keep no images in history · N = keep N most recent
# NOT COMMENTED OUT, DELIBERATELY. This was 0 from the 2026-08-24 incident
# (INCIDENT_2026-08-24.md) until 2026-09-01, and the comment here required a
# deliberate decision with the image-cost work done first before changing it.
# That work is done and this is that decision.
#
# MEASURED on the pod, 2026-09-01 (scripts/probe-vision.py, against vLLM
# directly): 256px=110 tokens, 512px=380, 1024px=1406, 2048px=3080,
# 3072px=3080. The cost PLATEAUS at 3,080 because the encoder downscales, so
# no upload can cost more than that however large the file - 14.8% of a
# 20,768-token input budget. /tokenize agreed with usage.prompt_tokens to the
# token at every size, so the budget guard genuinely sees images.
#
# 1, not more: the image is needed for the turn that asks about it; after
# that the assistant's description carries it forward as a durable fact and
# the pixels are pure cost.
#
# REQUIRES --mm-processor-cache-type shm in VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS. Without it the
# second image in a conversation triggers an assertion in vLLM's mirrored
# multimodal cache and the request 500s. See that variable's comment.
COMPACTOR_MAX_RETAINED_IMAGES=1
# An estimate, not a measurement — SET THIS CORRECTLY. v3.0.5 added a learned
# margin (main.py:194) that tightens after a vLLM rejection, but it is a
# backstop, not a substitute: it is process-global, capped at MAX_MODEL_LEN//4,
# never reset, and lost on restart. Real Mistral3 vision tiling is 4-8k per
# photo. Do not rely on the margin to correct a wrong value here.
# COMPACTOR_IMAGE_TOKENS=4096
# Only needed for gated HF repos (Llama, etc). Cydonia and Magnum are not gated.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Failure-alert webhook (boot self-test + backup daemon POST here on FAILURE).
#
# ALERTING IS INERT WHILE THIS IS COMMENTED OUT. alert.py:35 returns False
# when it is unset and every caller downstream no-ops. That includes all of
# v3.1 V3's new backup alerts — the missing-store failure, the collapsed
# payload, the census regression — which are dead code until a URL is set
# here. They are still correct (they refuse to publish and refuse to prune);
# they just tell nobody. This system has no other outbound failure signal:
# every failure in it is currently detected by the user noticing that the
# model has forgotten her, which is the direct cause of the ~10-hour
# detection time in the 2026-08-24 incident. (v3.1 P0-1 / F13.)
#
# Any Slack/Discord incoming-webhook URL or generic receiver works.
# COMPACTOR_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
